  "title": "Order of Operations",
  "body": " Order of Operations   Name:  When evaluating mathematical expressions, we follow a standard order so that everyone arrives at the same result.  1. Parentheses: Evaluate expressions inside grouping symbols such as parentheses . A fraction bar also acts as a grouping symbol, so you must simplify the entire numerator and the entire denominator first.  2. Exponents: Evaluate all powers.  3. Multiplication and Division: Work from left to right.  4. Addition and Subtraction: Work from left to right.    Learning Target Questions   Evaluate the following expressions step-by-step without using an electronic tool. Be sure to treat the fraction bar as a grouping symbol where appropriate, and show all intermediate steps to illustrate your reasoning.                                   Error Analysis   Two students evaluated the expression . Their work is shown below.    Student A       Student B       Assess their work. Only one solution is correct. Which student is correct? Identify the specific mathematical error made by the other student, and explain why that step violates the standard order of operations.    Student B is correct. Student A evaluated before applying the exponent, then cubed that result to reach . The exponent must be evaluated first, which gives . After the exponent, addition and subtraction are performed from left to right: , and then .     Parentheses Placement   The placement of parentheses can completely change the value of an expression. Consider the following:   Insert parentheses into this expression in two different ways to create two expressions with different final results. Show your step-by-step evaluation for both to verify your results.     Expression 1: write your first version, then evaluate it step-by-step.    Answers will vary. One possibility:         Expression 2: write a second version (with a different result), then evaluate it step-by-step.    Answers will vary. One possibility:        "
